Igor Natanzon <sysadmin@homer.bus.miami.edu> WROTE:

2. X-windows also truncates the full hostname stripping off the domain. 
So you'll have oak instead of oak.oakland.edu
That, however, doesn't work for TTYS which means you'll need to turn off 
that feature of xdm. (Putting the truncated hostname in ttys doesn't work)
So edit the file /var/X11/xdm/xdm-config and either add or replace the 
line that deals with hostnames: 
This is what you need to have in the file to turn off truncation.
DisplayManager.removeDomainname: false
It is very possible that this step is uncessesary but that's what worked 
for me.

