Dear Gurus,

1) First question: how to prevent my lasercolor, hooked to the parallel
   port of my alpha box, to be the "default" printer?
   Answer: this printer should NOT be called "lp" or "lp0" in 
           /etc/printcap.
           A printer called "lp" will be the default, unless you have
           defined a PRINTER environment variable.
           It is said also that the FIRST printer in /etc/printcap is
           considered as the default. This is true: before I
           installed the lasercolor as "lp", I received from time to 
           time some garbage on "my" printer which is the first one in
           printcap.

